   "description": "Pan-Tompkins style, zero-phase: 10-25 Hz band-pass (above the classic 5-15 Hz because tall exercise T waves dominated that band), derivative, squaring, centred 150 ms moving integration. Peaks at least 0.25 s apart above noise + 0.25 x (beat level - noise), with beat level the 10 s running median of 2 s maxima and noise the 10 s running median. Search-back for gaps over 1.66 x the local median interval at half threshold; a peak less than 0.36 s after a beat with under half its maximum slope is dropped as a T wave."
