   "description": "Wavelet and matched template: geometric mean of the Mexican-hat wavelet moduli at 6, 10 and 16 ms scales gives QRS candidates; the strongest candidates of each 60 s block form a median QRS template (+-60 ms, 5-40 Hz ECG). Beats are peaks of the normalised cross-correlation with that template above 0.6, at least 0.25 s apart, whose wavelet product within +-30 ms reaches 0.3 x the median of the template beats (rejects T waves, which match in shape but lack fine-scale energy), with search-back down to correlation 0.35 and wavelet ratio 0.2 for gaps over 1.6 x the local median interval."
  }
